[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: The latest change adds cancellation, elapsed-deadline, per-node timeout, and permanently-blocked-dependent cases, but three contracted behaviors remain unasserted: cancel invoked directly on a runner whose nodes are still non-terminal must set the cancellation status and mark every non-terminal node CANCELLED without any node action running; execution whose timeout budget is already exhausted when scheduling begins must raise DAGTimeoutError rather than dispatch a wave; and cancellation requested while a node action is still executing must mark running nodes CANCELLED and raise DAGCancelledError. Add unit tests asserting these postconditions through the public contract.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine/lib/dag_engine_impl.py: Resolve coverage feedback: restructured the DAGRunner scheduling loop into 'while True' with the cancellation guard evaluated at the start of every iteration before the scheduler.is_finished() test, and removed the now-redundant post-wave cancellation guard; loop now breaks explicitly on is_finished, so wave-entry cancellation is reachable and observed even when cancel() already drove every non-terminal node to CANCELLED. Verified mid-wave cancel, in-node cancel, overall/per-node timeouts, retries, all failure policies, concurrency limits, empty graphs, and post-cancel reruns still behave per contract
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/dag_engine/tests/dag_engine_impl_test.py: Add direct-cancel, exhausted-budget, and running-node cancellation coverage: runner.cancel() on still non-terminal nodes marks every READY/PENDING node CANCELLED and dispatches no action (including on a subsequent run); a run whose timeout budget is already exhausted before scheduling raises DAGTimeoutError without dispatching a wave; and cancellation requested from another thread while a gated node action is executing marks the running node and its unstarted dependents CANCELLED and raises DAGCancelledError
